<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Caleb Madrigal</title><link href="https://calebmadrigal.com/" rel="alternate"></link><link href="https://calebmadrigal.com/feeds/misc.atom.xml" rel="self"></link><id>https://calebmadrigal.com/</id><updated>2012-08-16T16:02:05-05:00</updated><entry><title>Vim run current file</title><link href="https://calebmadrigal.com/vim-run-current-file/" rel="alternate"></link><updated>2012-08-16T16:02:05-05:00</updated><author><name>Caleb Madrigal</name></author><id>tag:calebmadrigal.com,2012-08-16:vim-run-current-file/</id><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;I just added a nice command to my .vimrc file to allow me to run the current file I am working on by typing &lt;code&gt;:R&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;command R !./%
&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;On the VIM note, here is a link to my current vim config (.vimrc file and .vim directory) on github: &lt;a href="https://github.com/calebmadrigal/caleb-vim-config"&gt;Vim config&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><title>Barcamp Milwaukee 2012</title><link href="https://calebmadrigal.com/barcamp-milwaukee-2012/" rel="alternate"></link><updated>2012-08-15T14:44:29-05:00</updated><author><name>Caleb Madrigal</name></author><id>tag:calebmadrigal.com,2012-08-15:barcamp-milwaukee-2012/</id><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://barcampmilwaukee.org/"&gt;Barcamp Milwaukee&lt;/a&gt; 2012 is being held October 6th-7th.  I had a good time last year, so I can definitely recommend it :)&lt;/p&gt;</summary><category term="conferences"></category><category term="milwaukee"></category></entry></feed>